## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict PM4-1: The automated test asserts the opposite: a toolbar create is the default size in scene units, so its screen size scales with zoom.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/hooks/canvas/useDocumentCommands.ts#useDocumentCommands, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/utils/shapes.ts#nominalSize, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/hooks/canvas/useNodeDrop.ts#useNodeDrop]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/playwright/create.spec.ts]
  note: |
    `create.spec.ts` "a toolbar create is the default size in scene units whatever the zoom" expects width = nominal size x zoom. The code sizes a dropped or toolbar create as `nominalSize(def.defaultSize, cell)`, with no division by camera zoom. The depth step is not automated either.
```

```mdl
verdict PM4-2: create.spec.ts checks a 240x160 sweep within a cell and that a motionless press creates nothing.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/hooks/canvas/usePointerMachine.ts#usePointerMachine]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/playwright/create.spec.ts]
  note: |
    The wide-box and click-without-moving steps are automated. The small 120x80 box step is not.
```

```mdl
verdict PM4-3: Snapping after a hard zoom-out is automated; drilled-in snapping and G hiding the grid are not.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/hooks/canvas/useSceneSnap.ts#sceneSnap]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/playwright/create.spec.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/playwright/scene.spec.ts]
  note: |
    `create.spec.ts` covers the zoom-out nudge and `scene.spec.ts` the move and resize landing on the major grid. No test drags inside a portal, checks edges against drawn lines, or presses G and asserts the grid disappears.
```

```mdl
verdict PM4-4: The zoom readout after a drill-in is not exercised by any test.
  status: missing
  note: |
    The flow is marked manual. No Playwright or unit test reads the toolbar percentage across a drill-in; searched `src/playwright` and `*.test.ts`.
```

```mdl
verdict PM4-5: Body-to-body linking and hover-only ports are automated; port precedence and refused ends are not.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/hooks/canvas/usePointerMachine.ts#usePointerMachine]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/playwright/scene.spec.ts]
  note: |
    `scene.spec.ts` checks that ports show only on the hovered node (with no tool picked, not with L) and that the line tool links two bodies without adding a node. No test drops near a port to check it wins, or drops on a node whose ports all refuse the end.
```

```mdl
verdict PM4-6: route.test.ts checks the stub geometry and the same-side double-back; drawing with O and live re-routing are not automated.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/utils/route.ts#smartPoints, github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/utils/route.ts#linkPath]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/ui/react-ui-canvas/src/utils/route.test.ts]
  note: |
    The geometry steps are unit-tested through `smartPoints`. No browser test draws a smart link or moves a linked node; `demo.spec.ts` does both but asserts nothing.
```

```mdl
verdict PM4-7: Text size at depth and the fontSize override are not exercised by any test.
  status: missing
  note: |
    The flow is marked manual. `properties.test.ts` only lists `fontSize` among the editable fields; nothing checks the rendered text size or that the size class is dropped.
